	"naming": {
		"_about": "Names from long-time holders (Items.naming, decision 365). A thing with a verb, or tagged armour or tool, carried by one named holder (a player, a companion) held_days of the world clock (DayNight.day_steps; while they are in the world) with deeds or more done with it, or deeds_alone however long (decision 472: a season, or 20 deeds), earns its character (only then does it count kills and grow, 415, 417) and takes a name for life from lore's forms, and one strength: the one whose from is the deed its namer did most with it. Each strength changes how its verb works, never its damage: guard_stamina (times what guarding costs), draw (times a bow's draw times), brace_ticks (the steps still before a spear is braced), noise (times the fight noise of its blows), down_ticks (added to a knockdown), dread (World.holder_dread: enemy-ai reads it). A deed with no strength (struck) gives none.",
		"held_days": 7.0,
		"deeds_alone": 20,
		"deeds": 10,
		"strengths": {
			"steady": {"from": "guarded", "guard_stamina": 0.75, "says": "guarding with it costs a quarter less stamina"},
			"quick": {"from": "shot", "draw": 0.8, "says": "it draws in four fifths of the time"},
			"set": {"from": "braced", "brace_ticks": 3, "says": "braced sooner"},
			"quiet": {"from": "behind", "noise": 0.5, "says": "its blows make half the fight noise"},
			"heavy": {"from": "downed", "down_ticks": 5, "says": "its knockdowns last half a second longer"},
			"dread": {"from": "felled", "dread": true, "says": "cowards dread whoever holds it"}
		}
	},
	"growth": {
		"_about": "Bane and vengeance (decision 417). A thing that has felled bane_after of one kind (ItemBook's tally, decision 415) is that kind's bane for life: that kind dreads its bearer and notices them bane_notice times further (World.holder_bane; enemy-ai reads it). Only a thing with character grows (decision 472), and only one way (decision 473): a thing whose holders one kind has hurt grudge_after hp, more than any other kind, takes a grudge against it (none once it is a bane, and becoming one drops its grudge): its blows stagger that kind grudge_stagger ticks, and that kind seeks its bearer first (World.holder_grudge; enemy-ai); grudge_paid of that kind felled with it, the grudge lifts and that kind's hurt starts over.",
		"bane_after": 25,
		"bane_notice": 1.5,
		"grudge_after": 30,
		"grudge_stagger": 4,
		"grudge_paid": 5,
		"says": {"bane": "its kind dread whoever holds it, and notice them from further off", "vengeance": "its blows stagger that kind, and they come for whoever holds it first"}
	},
	"curse": {
		"_about": "Cursed heirlooms (Items.curse, decision 370). A named thing taken by anyone but its namer, other than from the namer's own hand (off the ground, out of a chest or the stockpile, from a monster's spill), is kept from its namer until it is back in the namer's hands. While kept, a holder it counts for gathers ill, 0 to 1 over full_days of the world clock held, and loses it at fade of that rate while not holding it. follows: thing (every holder but the namer) or taker (only who took it); Jeff's question, thing until he answers. below_baseline: whether ill may take the holder below baseline (true: noticed farther off, slower mending) or only shortens their buffs (false); null until Jeff answers, and until then ill does nothing.",
		"follows": "thing",
		"below_baseline": null,
		"full_days": 1.0,
		"fade": 0.5
	}
}
